 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Threshold is -0.4 to -1.0 V (typically -0.7 V) at -250 μA with gate and drain tied. On-resistance is specified at two gate drives: 112 mΩ max at -4.5 V and -2.8 A, 142 mΩ max at -2.5 V and -2.0 A. It climbs with drain current and with temperature: normalized on-resistance is about 0.7 at -50 °C and about 1.55 at 150 °C. The gate withstands ±8 V; leakage there is at most ±100 nA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With -4.5 V drive, -10 V on the drain, -1 A and a 1 Ω gate resistor, turn-on delay is 11 ns typ and rise 35 ns typ; turn-off delay is 30 ns typ and fall 10 ns typ. Total gate charge is 5.5 nC typ (10 nC max) at -4.5 V drive and 3.3 nC typ (6 nC max) at -2.5 V. The body diode drops at most -1.2 V at -0.70 A and recovers in 13.1 ns typ at -2.3 A and 100 A/μs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Junction-to-ambient thermal resistance is 312 °C/W in steady state, and junction and storage temperature span -55 °C to +150 °C. The maximum continuous drain current is about 2.4 A up to 25 °C ambient and falls to zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Built on a low-voltage trench process with a dense cell layout. The SOT-23 molding is UL 94V-0 rated, RoHS-compliant and halogen-free; the leads are solder plated and pass the MIL-STD-750 method 2026 solderability test."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Listed uses are battery-powered systems, solid-state relays and direct interfacing to TTL or CMOS logic levels; switching is described as high speed."
